,{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"°, like Unicode 00B0 half-diminished: ø, like Unicode 00F8"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the major-minor kind, only the minor symbol is used when use-symbols is yes. The major symbol is set using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the symbol attribute in the degree-value element. The corresponding degree-alter value will usually be 0 in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this case."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The text attribute describes how the kind should be spelled in a score. If use-symbols is yes, the value of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the text attribute follows the symbol. The stack-degrees attribute is yes if the degree elements should be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stacked above each other. The parentheses-degrees attribute is yes if all the degrees should be in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parentheses. The bracket-degrees attribute is yes if all the degrees should be in a bracket. If not specified,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"these values are implementation-specific. The alignment attributes are for the entire harmony-chord group of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which this kind element is a part."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The text attribute may use strings such as “13sus” that refer to both the kind and one or more degree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements. In this case, the corresponding degree elements should have the print-object attribute set to “no”"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to keep redundant alterations from being displayed."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Kind indicates the type of chord. Degree elements can then add, subtract, or alter from these starting points."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony\/Chord-swift.struct\/Kind-swift.struct"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharmony\/chord-swift.struct\/kind-swift.struct"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHarmony/Chord-swift.struct/Kind-swift.struct/usesSymbols":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether the kind should be represented when possible with harmony symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than letters and numbers."}],"title":"usesSymbols","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony\/Chord-swift.struct\/Kind-swift.struct\/usesSymbols","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharmony\/chord-swift.struct\/kind-swift.struct\/usessymbols","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"usesSymbols"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/SQ":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","title":"Swift.Equatable"},"doc://IvorMXL/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHarmony/Chord-swift.struct/Kind-swift.struct/font":{"title":"font","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"font","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFont","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharmony\/chord-swift.struct\/kind-swift.struct\/font","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony\/Chord-swift.struct\/Kind-swift.struct\/font","abst